WEBVTT

00:06:30.833 --> 00:06:32.101
Because, let's face it,

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:35.726
right now we all want
more powerful and faster phones.

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:39.917
Well, more power and faster
requires more circuitry.

00:06:41.333 --> 00:06:43.018
So how do we do this?

00:06:43.042 --> 00:06:46.768
It's not like we have some magic
electromagnetic shrink ray,

00:06:46.792 --> 00:06:49.851
like professor Wayne Szalinski used
in "Honey, I Shrunk the Kids"

00:06:49.875 --> 00:06:51.226
to shrink his children.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:52.542
On accident, of course.

00:06:53.792 --> 00:06:55.042
Or do we?

00:06:55.958 --> 00:06:57.726
Well, actually, in the field,

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:00.476
there's a process
that's pretty similar to that.